Hi,

My company's IT protocol requires a 3 tier server architecture (with firewalls separating the servers). One tier is the database, 2nd tier is the application and the 3rd tier is the web server. This is for security reasons.

In this case, how can I go about having this hosting set up for R Shiny? Currently, we host our R Shiny dashboard internally and our web server, app and database sit on the same server. I host the website internally by running runApp(file = <file name>, host = "<Server IP address>", port = <port no.>) on R studio. I'm not sure how the back end works in R shiny in order to split into three tiers.

Thank you.

